   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bait is required to fish. Open your inventory and craft some bait from the handcrafting menu. <br><br>Once crafted, equip your fishing rod and load the bait onto it the same way you would load arrows onto a bow."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A847B2674FF7ED2303D708A6827928ED",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Catch a Fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "FDBD97FB4524B1F7F8BCAD8532016503",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Equip your fishing rod and approach any body of water. Use Start Fishing in your emotes radial menu (default: R) to cast your line, then wait for a fish to bite. <br><br>When the mini-game starts, keep the fish inside the capture zone until the progress bar fills to reel it in. (Press LMB to go up, release to go down)"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "997CFE404B9D829C722D9A943BC07BA9",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Cook a Fish Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "4F7F5C194C312FD6743BE8856B80DCC3",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Caught fish can be processed into fillets at the Stove. Fillets are used as ingredients to craft higher-tier fishing equipment and bait. <br><br>Different fish yield different fillets depending on their biome and tier."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "8AA7374741352F1531ED188CE4308C06",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Craft a piece of Fisher's Equipment"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DB2BFF7C4DDA3FC4B8484081F2A06788",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fisher's equipment is crafted at the Armorer's Bench. Each piece increases your Fishing Power, which improves your odds of catching rarer fish and reduces the time between bites. <br><br>Fisher's equipment occupies your armor slots."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A4EF09894E204FB8C899DA8B33B8766B",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Craft a Fishing Accessory"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DA85258B4D1888A53A4213AEC6BD7A73",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fishing accessories are crafted at the Tinker's Bench. They provide passive bonuses while fishing and do not need to be equipped, simply keep them in your inventory. <br><br>Only one of each accessory is counted. Carrying duplicates provides no additional benefit."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "9A90523648F8DCE7BA9688BA66F9DFED",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "MISSED"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "45CC209847B5CB588C93DFB8BD12285B",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "GOOD"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "3E263A6B4057AE6757E662A5E5ECBBA3",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "???"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "CDD6E8CC4458F85A02BC05944EAF78E4",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "6C17DC4A4BBF54336D755483D3CA510D",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "F8E6B4FF40BFA27E30EA9395818121AD",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": ", {0}"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "821217BC47A41193983663A6FE1DEA12",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "{Charges}/{Max}"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "44CC6AA84706130038202F88E51088A2",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Food buff potency: strength of the stat bonuses given by the fish dishes and feasts of this mod. 100 % = unchanged, 50 % = half, 0 % = no bonus. Applies from the next dish eaten; item descriptions keep showing the base values."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "AECA59A94303E35C5D412B95820BC1A2",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Reset to Vanilla. Press Apply to send it to the server."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "027113AB46A587E1A06812AF64C9157A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sent to the server. Every player receives the new settings right away."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A2D0416B40542CB613325D8FC9B4D995",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Profile loaded into the panel. Press Apply to send it to the server."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "31531FCF44103E0CA0BC0BBA39C00A04",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "This profile slot is empty."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "B8E871894468566ECC4A19B720DA0320",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Profile saved on the server (the settings shown in this panel)."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "AED71B2B4C45DA33054F9DB475A00575",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Profile deleted on the server."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "0F02D2C84E4BC41B28F93F8F0AA184DC",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Overall difficulty for every player. Vanilla = the original game. Easy = more fish of the player's own level; rare fish stay rare."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "5D5A43FB452568B2FD36D89FB651E9BB",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Custom: edit the drop weight of each fish in the list, on top of the difficulty chosen here. Higher = more frequent, 0 = never caught. Click again to go back to the plain difficulty."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "7472085C4EC75ADF63BFC1B6C66F7156",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Catch focus: boosts fish whose required Fishing Power is close to the player's, at the expense of fish far below it (junk, low tiers). 0 = vanilla odds."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "37AFDA5849609DEF8EBD6788EF98B5B6",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Level tolerance: width of the at-level window. Low = only fish very close to the player's Fishing Power are boosted. High = a wider range."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "F6E8D3B54368AEFE80036588480D46D8",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Mythic (T7) rarity: multiplier on Mythic fish only (inside their time window). 1 = unchanged, 0.5 = half as often."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "C4801BE5401C76F0FBCFE2A5501A397A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bite wait: multiplies the wait before a bite. 0.5 = twice as fast. 1 = vanilla."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "49CD65064309ECDDEDCEEDA3C18D86EC",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fight difficulty: difficulty of the catch mini-game. Below 1 = easier fights."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "59B86E66421C77D33273D487139F5C75",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fish speed: how fast the fish moves in the mini-game. Below 1 = slower."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A5BD4B3948BC9301E011098F4EDAF2E8",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Catch zone: size of the catch zone in the mini-game. Above 1 = bigger, easier."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "CB17B3C04730200D32B4C8AF996F867D",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fishing Power of the test fisher used by the simulator."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "B24BA40448DFE17C33FABD91B9AD7799",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Biome where the test fisher is fishing."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A13496C04763288D68AD44AFFE70A0DB",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "C7352FE24139D37288B15C8BC70671D1",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "B5DE05F746D1B8CFE63FB9AE0E22F451",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "FAE32114406E83982B916DA9080AA8B6",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Time of day of the test fisher."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "95C0EA9C4F1925D3643D85A9282428FE",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "BFBD53644ED131A441B8BDAE0F40269A",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "B56B0B2E4BBE9BBEA90845830A592907",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "90DB41CD4DFEB108CDA39899092ED25F",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Simulate the Barbed Hook (halves junk)."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "C0B76AB446C60111BC2AAE819866109A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Simulate the Mythic hour: Mythic fish can only bite inside their time window."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "013D39024F88B45B7C678FA26D81B2CA",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Rough estimate: about 20 s per fight plus the average bite wait."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "CCC5C8BD425CE1DE250EB988D70C2E61",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Send these settings to the server. Every player gets them at once, and they are saved."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "212FB9424A1C02E32BA6D2AA453B395F",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Back to the original game for everything (difficulty, fine tuning and fish weights). Press Apply to send."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "7A1723704E013C936B6EAF8F1ACA103C",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Name used when you press Save."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "F54382BF4082626EE7240A90EE33A7F5",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Save the settings shown in this panel into the selected slot, on the server. Overwrites the slot."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "B2432DFF4278F7DEBFA098955D1AE7D0",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Load the selected profile into the panel. Nothing changes on the server until you press Apply."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "855A5F5F470CE83A4DDB6DA964F441F8",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Delete the selected profile on the server."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "B26C4F674C0F46569E8958B697E6C11B",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The basics of fishing. Craft your first rod and learn to prepare the most common catches."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389401_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Angler"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389402_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A seasoned fisher who has learned to work with rarer catches and craft superior gear."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389402_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Master Angler"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389403_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A master of the craft who bends the waters to their will, luring fish from any biome."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389403_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Legendary Angler"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389404_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Few ever reach this level. Those who do can craft tools worthy of the rarest creatures in the depths."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389404_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fisher Cooking"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389406_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Learn simple meals made from common fishing fillets."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389406_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Angler Cooking"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389407_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Learn practical meals made from uncommon fishing fillets."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389407_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Master Angler Cooking"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389408_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Learn expedition meals made from rare and epic fishing fillets."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389408_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Legendary Angler Cooking"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389409_FeatName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Learn elite meals made from legendary and mythic fishing fillets."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_FeatTable_389409_Description",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Old Boot"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388001_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A worn-out boot. Not exactly what you were fishing for."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388001_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Exiles have a saying: the river gives what the river chooses. Today, it chose to give back something it had no use for. Neither do you."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388001_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Wet Branch"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388002_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A soggy branch pulled from the water. Better luck next time."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388002_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The river is patient. It has swallowed whole cities and returned nothing but silence. Today it returned this. You are not sure what that means."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388002_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Silverscale"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388003_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A small, silvery fish found in waters across the Exiled Lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388003_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "So common it has no legend, no name in the old tongues. And yet it has outlasted every empire that ever tried to dam the rivers it calls home. There is something to be said for that."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388003_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Underestimated by every predator in the river, and yet it persists in vast numbers where larger fish have long since vanished. Soldiers and scholars alike could learn something from the minnow."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388004_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Pale Darter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388005_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A slender freshwater fish with pale, shimmering scales. Darts away at the slightest disturbance."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388005_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It vanishes before you can be certain you have seen it. Some scholars argue the Pale Darter is not one species but many or perhaps just a trick of the light on moving water. The exiles who catch them disagree."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388005_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Common Catfish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388006_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A whiskered bottom-feeder. Prefers murky waters."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388006_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It asks nothing of the world but mud and darkness, and the world obliges. The catfish has fed exiles through famines, wars, and worse. It receives no gratitude. It does not seem to mind."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388006_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Common Carp"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388007_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A sturdy freshwater fish. Puts up a decent fight."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388007_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Old river folk say a carp does not die easily because it has too much stubbornness to yield. They are not wrong. A hooked carp will fight longer than most men would bother to."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388007_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Common Eel"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388008_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A slippery creature that emerges at dusk. Hard to hold onto."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388008_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "No one has ever seen an eel spawn. No one knows where they come from or where they go. The river keeps its secrets, and the eel is chief among them."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388008_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Desert Perch"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388010_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A hardy fish adapted to the warm waters of the southern rivers."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388010_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Where the rivers run shallow and hot and most fish retreat or perish, the Desert Perch thrives. The exiles of the south consider it a symbol of endurance, small, stubborn, and impossible to be rid of."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388010_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Butterfly Fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388011_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A colorful fish with wing-like fins. Floats gracefully near the surface."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388011_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "In the courts of the south, merchants once paid handsomely for Butterfly Fish kept alive in ornamental pools. The Exiled Lands have no courts left. The fish did not notice."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388011_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Barracuda"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388012_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fierce predator with razor-sharp teeth. Strikes with blinding speed."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388012_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A Hyborian sailor's proverb holds that the barracuda strikes once, perfectly, and asks no forgiveness. Many a fisherman has pulled one aboard only to discover the meaning of that saying firsthand."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388012_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Boxfish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388013_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An oddly shaped fish encased in bony plates. Slow but resilient."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388013_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Nature's great joke: a creature so thoroughly armored it can barely swim, and yet it outlives nearly everything that tries to eat it. The Exiled Lands have a great many such creatures."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388013_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Golden Piranha"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388014_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A vicious little fish with a golden sheen. Hunts in packs."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388014_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Alone, a curiosity. In numbers, a catastrophe. Desert tribes have long used shoals of Golden Piranha as execution pits. The condemned were given one minute to pray. It was more than enough time for the fish."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388014_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Royal Grouper"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388015_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive fish that lurks in deep, warm waters. Prized by fishermen."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388015_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient kings of the south kept Royal Grouper as living trophies, believing their vast size was an omen of prosperity. Their kingdoms are ruins. The grouper are still here."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388015_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Scorpionfish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388016_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A venomous fish disguised among the rocks. Handle with extreme care."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388016_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It does not chase. It does not hunt. It simply waits, perfectly still among the stones, and lets the world come to it. A philosophy that has served it well for longer than men have had philosophies."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388016_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Golden Ray"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388017_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A majestic creature that glides through warm currents at twilight."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388017_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The old coastal priests called it the Veil of the Setting Sun, a creature that belonged neither to the water nor the dying light, but to the threshold between them. It appears as dusk falls, and is gone before full dark."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388017_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Styx Carp"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388018_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A pale fish found in cursed waters. Said to ferry souls across the river."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388018_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The dying sometimes report seeing pale shapes beneath dark water in their final moments. Priests dismiss it as delirium. Fishermen who have pulled a Styx Carp from a black river at night are less certain."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388018_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Solar Eel"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388019_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A luminous eel that surfaces only at dawn. Its skin glows faintly."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388019_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Followers of the flame-cults believe the Solar Eel carries a fragment of the sun's fire in its flesh, trapped there during the world's first dawn and never extinguished. They do not eat it. Exiles do."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388019_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Arid Moonfish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388020_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A ghostly fish that appears under the desert moon. Extremely elusive."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388020_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Desert monks who keep vigil through the night have written of a fish that surfaces only when both moons are reflected in the water. They offer no explanation. Neither does the fish."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388020_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sand Moray"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388021_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A terrifying eel that burrows in desert riverbeds. Strikes from the shadows."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388021_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It does not need to see you. It senses the warmth of your hand in the water, the pressure of your step on the bank. Desert fishermen have a rule: never reach into a river at night. The Sand Moray is the reason."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388021_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sand Dragon"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388022_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A creature of legend. Ancient texts speak of a serpent that swims through sand and water alike. Only appears at the break of dawn."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388022_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Pre-Hyborian tablets describe it as the First Swimmer; a creature that predates the rivers themselves, that carved the desert channels with its passage. Most scholars call this myth. Those scholars fish in safer waters than you."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388022_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Common Trout"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388023_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A reliable catch found in temperate streams. A staple for any fisherman."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388023_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "There is a kind of dignity in the ordinary. The trout asks nothing of fortune, demands no special hour or secret depth. It is simply there, as it has always been, feeding exiles who know where to look."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388023_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River Perch"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388024_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A striped fish found in calm rivers. Easy to catch, hard to resist."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388024_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Every exile who has eaten well beside a temperate river has eaten perch. It is the taste of a good day, of sun on water, of a moment when the Exiled Lands felt, briefly, like home."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388024_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Stone Roach"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388025_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A small, hardy fish that hides among the stones of temperate rivers."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388025_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The Stone Roach survives by being beneath notice. It hides where larger creatures cannot follow, feeds on what others ignore, and outlasts everything that overlooks it. A lesson the wise exile takes to heart."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388025_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Rivershine"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388026_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A tiny bottom-dweller whose scales catch the light like gold dust."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388026_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River traders once sold Rivershine scales as counterfeit gold to the desperate and the gullible. The practice stopped when a merchant discovered the buyer had not, in fact, been fooled, and had simply been waiting for the right moment to collect his debt."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388026_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Golden Koi"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388027_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An ornate fish with brilliant golden patterns. Prized by collectors."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388027_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Once bred in the garden pools of noble houses, tended by servants, admired by poets. The houses are gone. The poets are gone. The Golden Koi still drifts through river bends as if it owns them. Perhaps it does."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388027_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Barbel"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388028_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A strong river fish with sensitive barbels. Feeds at dawn and dusk."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388028_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River fishermen in the old kingdoms considered catching a Barbel a test of patience and skill, a fish that does not rush, and therefore cannot be rushed. It comes when it comes. Not before."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388028_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Pike"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388029_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An ambush predator with a fearsome jaw. Lurks among the reeds."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388029_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River villages nail Pike jaws above doorways as wards against evil. Whether this works against evil is uncertain. It definitely works against small children wandering too close to the reeds."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388029_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Green Tench"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388030_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A slimy, bottom-dwelling fish coated in green mucus. Surprisingly tasty."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388030_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Physicians of the old world believed Tench mucus had healing properties and prescribed bathing in water where Tench had been kept. Patients often recovered. Whether it was the Tench or simply the bath remains a matter of debate."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388030_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zander"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388031_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A nocturnal predator with glassy eyes. Hunts in the fading light."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388031_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It does its best work in the hours when men grow uncertain and careless. River hunters say the Zander and the thief share the same philosophy: wait for the light to fail, then move."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388031_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Silver Salmon"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388032_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A powerful fish that leaps upstream at dawn. A true test of skill."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388032_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The old kingdom fishermen held that catching a Silver Salmon at first light was an omen of a great day ahead. Given how hard the fish fights, simply landing one without losing your footing probably qualifies."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388032_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River Serpent"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388033_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A sinuous creature that coils through deep waters. More snake than fish."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388033_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River people argue endlessly about where the eel ends and the River Serpent begins. The distinction matters less than you might think once one has coiled itself around your arm in three feet of dark water."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388033_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Nocturnal Char"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388034_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rare fish that feeds only in total darkness. Its scales absorb light."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388034_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fishermen who have caught it describe the experience as hauling something out of a dream; a fish that seems to belong to the dark rather than the water. It does not thrash. It simply stares, as if it is the one doing the catching."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388034_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Whiskered King"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388035_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An enormous catfish said to have lived for centuries. Rules the riverbed."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388035_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River villages speak of a catfish so old that the grandfathers of grandfathers tried and failed to catch it. They say it remembers the old kingdoms. They say it has swallowed men who disturbed its rest. They may be right on both counts."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388035_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "King of Rivers"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388036_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The undisputed lord of temperate waters. Legends say it can only be caught when the sun is at its peak."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388036_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It appears only at the height of noon, when shadows vanish and the river is pure light. Ancient texts describe it as the river made visible, not a fish at all, but the water itself given a moment of form. Whatever it is, it will not come for you until you have earned it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388036_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Whitefish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388037_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A cold-water fish with pale, flaky flesh. Abundant in northern lakes."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388037_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The northern exiles say if you find Whitefish in a lake, the lake is good. Clean water, healthy depth, nothing cursed below. They use it as a scout fish. It has never led them wrong."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388037_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ice Trout"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388038_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trout adapted to freezing waters. Its blood resists the cold."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388038_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Northern healers once studied Ice Trout blood in search of a remedy for frostbite. They found nothing medically useful, but they did find it was very good to eat, which resolved the problem in a different way entirely."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388038_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Glacier Perch"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388039_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A small perch that thrives beneath glacial waters."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388039_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It lives in water cold enough to kill a man in minutes, feeds on life forms invisible to the naked eye, and asks for nothing more. The northern exiles admire it enormously and do not apologize for eating it anyway."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388039_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Winter Smelt"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388040_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A tiny fish that swims in schools beneath the ice. Active at dawn and night."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388040_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "In the deep north, when the ice is too thick and the cold too fierce for any sensible creature, the Winter Smelt moves in vast silent schools beneath the frozen surface. Exiles who learn to fish them through the ice rarely go hungry."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388040_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fjord Fera"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388041_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A sleek fish that glides through deep fjord waters at dusk."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388041_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The northern clans named it after the Fera, their word for a blade that cuts without resistance. They mean it as a compliment. Any fish that moves through ice-cold water with that kind of ease has earned the comparison."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388041_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Arctic Pike"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388042_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A savage predator of frozen lakes. Its strikes are as cold as the water."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388042_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Where the southern pike is a river bully, the Arctic Pike is something more deliberate. It holds perfectly still under the ice, sometimes for hours, until what it wants swims close enough. Then it moves once. That is enough."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388042_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Arctic Char"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388043_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A beautifully spotted fish of the frozen north. Prized for its taste."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388043_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Northern hunters consider the Arctic Char a gift from the ice itself, too beautiful to catch casually, too good to leave behind. It is the fish most likely to be offered at feasts and most likely to cause arguments over who gets the last piece."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388043_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Snow Cod"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388044_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A heavy fish that sinks to the deepest, coldest depths. Surfaces at twilight."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388044_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It spends its life in the deepest cold, feeding on what sinks to the bottom of frozen lakes. It rises only at dusk, briefly, as if checking whether the world above the ice is worth anything. It never seems convinced."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388044_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Northern Salmon"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388045_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A powerful salmon that battles upstream through icy rapids at dawn."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388045_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "There is an old northern saying: the salmon does not ask whether the current is fair. It simply goes. Exiles who have watched a Northern Salmon fight its way upstream through ice and white water tend to find the saying less poetic and more accurate than expected."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388045_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Arctic Grayling"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388046_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A delicate fish with a sail-like dorsal fin. A rare dawn catch."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388046_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It rises to the surface only at the precise moment when night concedes to morning, a window measured in minutes, not hours. Northern poets called it the Herald of the Dawn. Northern fishermen call it the most frustrating catch in the frozen lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388046_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Frozen Sturgeon"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388047_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An ancient armored fish, massive and slow. Its roe is worth a fortune."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388047_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A Frozen Sturgeon carries more history in its scales than most ruins. They have been here longer than the kingdoms that once fished them, longer than the exiles that replaced those kingdoms. They do not hurry. They have no reason to."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388047_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Abyssal Burbot"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388048_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A grotesque deep-water predator. Never sees the light of day."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388048_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Deep-water fishers who have hauled one up from the black describe a creature that seems confused by the surface, not frightened, not hostile, simply baffled by the concept of light, as if it has spent its entire existence certain that darkness was all there was."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388048_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ice Leviathan"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388049_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A colossal serpent of the frozen depths. It surfaces only at the stroke of midnight, when the ice cracks and the water turns black."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388049_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The northern clans do not fish for the Ice Leviathan. They leave offerings at the water's edge on the coldest nights, and in the morning the offerings are gone. They consider this a good outcome. Exiles from the south call it superstition — until they fish the northern waters at midnight. Most do not call it superstition after that."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388049_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Frog Fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388050_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A bizarre creature, half frog, half fish. Floats lazily on the surface."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388050_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp dwellers have a saying: if the Frog Fish is on the surface, the water below is safe. If it has disappeared, do not reach in to find out why. It is not a superstition. It is experience."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388050_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp Spawn"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388051_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A bloated larval creature born from the foulest swamp waters. It should not exist."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388051_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "No naturalist has successfully classified what it is, what it will become, or whether it is even the same creature from one sighting to the next. The swamp produces it in abundance, as if making a point no one asked for."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388051_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Mire Carp"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388052_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thick-scaled carp that feeds on swamp vegetation. Tough as leather."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388052_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It has absorbed everything the swamp has thrown at it for generations and emerged with scales like tanned hide and flesh that tastes accordingly. Swamp exiles eat it without complaint. They have eaten worse. They will eat worse again."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388052_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Mire Gulper"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388053_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fish that feeds on the foulest muck. Its mouth is always open, always hungry."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388053_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It consumes the swamp's filth and grows fat on it. In a place where nothing is wasted and everything rots, the Mire Gulper fills a role no other creature wants. The swamp rewards it accordingly."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388053_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient Bichir"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388054_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A living fossil from a forgotten age. Its armor-like scales predate the Exiled Lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388054_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Scholars who have studied the Ancient Bichir believe it has not changed in any meaningful way for tens of thousands of years. The swamp has changed. The world has changed. The Bichir has simply waited for everyone else to stop being dramatic about it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388054_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Viper Fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388055_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A needle-toothed horror from the darkest swamp waters. Bites first, asks never."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388055_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp hunters warn newcomers about it the same way they warn them about quicksand and fever: not to frighten, but because the warning is the difference between a story told later and no story at all."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388055_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp Catfish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388056_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A monstrous catfish that rules the swamp waters. Its whiskers sense everything."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388056_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Nothing enters its territory without its knowledge. The Swamp Catfish does not see with eyes, it reads the water itself, every ripple and tremor, every displacement of mud. It knew you were here before you arrived."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388056_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Mist Loach"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388057_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A ghostly fish that appears only in the morning mist. Gone by sunrise."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388057_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It exists in the window between night and morning, in the grey hour when the swamp exhales its fog. By the time the mist burns away, it has returned to wherever it comes from. Swamp folk who have caught one say it felt like catching something that was not quite there."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388057_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Lungfish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388058_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An ancient fish that can breathe air. Survives where others cannot."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388058_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "When the swamp dries and every other fish perishes, the Lungfish seals itself in a cocoon of mud and simply waits for the rains to return. It has been doing this since before the Hyborian Age. It expects to be doing it long after."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388058_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Putrid Piranha"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388059_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A piranha that feeds on rot and decay. Its bite carries disease."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388059_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Where its desert cousin hunts the living, the Putrid Piranha serves the dead. It cleans the swamp of what falls into it, consuming rot with ruthless efficiency. Swamp healers warn that a bite from one will fester within hours and claim the limb within days."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388059_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Black Lamprey"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388060_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A parasitic nightmare that latches on and never lets go. Pure darkness."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388060_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp shamans use Black Lamprey in ritual bloodletting, claiming the creature draws out corruption along with blood. Whether this is medicine or superstition depends on whether the patient survives. The survival rate is not discussed."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388060_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient of the Deep"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388061_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A primordial horror from the deepest swamp. It has waited in the dark since before the age of men."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388061_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The swamp tribes do not name it. To name a thing is to claim some power over it, and no one has ever held power over this. It has been in the deep channels since before the swamp existed, since before the land above the water had a name. It does not hunt. It simply endures, as it has always endured, as it will endure long after the last exile has turned to mud."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388061_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ghost Fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388062_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A translucent fish that drifts through the darkest waters like a living phantom."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388062_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Northern shamans claim the Ghost Fish is not a creature of the living world at all, but a soul that forgot to leave the river. They do not fish for it. Exiles who have seen one drift past their line in black water at midnight tend to leave it alone as well. Not out of reverence. Out of unease."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388062_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Plague Serpent"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388063_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A writhing abomination whose flesh carries disease. Even touching it invites death."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388063_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It is believed to be a creature changed by something older and fouler than the swamp itself, a corruption that runs deeper than rot. Exiles who have landed one and survived describe a sense of wrongness that does not fade for days. Some say it never entirely does."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_388063_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fisher's Cap"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389201_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_389201_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A wide-brimmed hat for patient anglers"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389201_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A simple straw hat that keeps the sun from your eyes while you wait for a bite. It offers minimal protection but contributes to your fishing prowess."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389201_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fishing Power +{0}"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389201_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389202_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389203_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389204_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389205_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389206_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389207_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389208_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389209_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389210_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389211_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389212_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389213_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389214_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389215_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389216_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
