    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389303_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Cut from a common warm-water fish and left to cure under the scorching desert sun. The process draws out the moisture and leaves something tough, stiff, and surprisingly resilient. Desert craftsmen discovered long ago that these strips, woven together, hold shape better than most leathers."
