    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Spiced Oasis Cut"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389305_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388015_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388016_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388017_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rare cut seasoned with oasis herbs"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389305_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A choice cut from one of the rarer warm-water species, prepared with herbs found only near desert oases. The curing process releases a scent so concentrated that it lingers long after preparation, a quality that certain craftsmen exploit with great effect."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389305_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Gilded Desert Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389306_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388018_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388019_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rich fillet from an epic warm-water fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389306_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thick, golden-fleshed fillet from one of the desert's most prized catches. The rendered oil carries something almost alchemical, it doesn't simply nourish, it coaxes. Experienced bait-makers say a single drop in the right preparation can draw creatures from depths that sunlight never reaches."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389306_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Solar Crowned Cut"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389307_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388020_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388021_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A legendary fillet glowing with warmth"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389307_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A cut from a creature few anglers will ever see. The flesh seems to retain warmth long after the catch, and the fibers (once rendered) carry a flexibility that no tanning process can replicate. Craftsmen who work with living wood speak of it in hushed tones."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389307_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Dragon-Flamed Slab"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389308_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388022_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A mythic slab from the Sand Dragon"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389308_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive slab torn from the Sand Dragon itself. The scales embedded in the flesh catch and scatter light in patterns that seem almost deliberate; shifting, flickering, drawing the eye from impossible distances. Some say it never truly stops shining."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389308_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River-Scraped Strip"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389309_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388023_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388024_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388025_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rough strip from a common river fish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389309_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A simple strip scraped from the flanks of a common highland river fish. Unremarkable on its own, but the cold river water these fish inhabit leaves the flesh dense and consistent, qualities that make it useful beyond the cooking fire."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389309_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River-Cured Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389310_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388026_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388027_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388028_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fillet cured in highland brine"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389310_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A clean fillet from the temperate highland rivers, cured in mountain brine. The salt process leaves the fibers unusually tough without becoming brittle. Highland armorers have long worked this property into their craft, it layers well and holds stitching better than most."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389310_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Smoked Highland Cut"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389311_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388029_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388030_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388031_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rare cut smoked over highland hardwood"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389311_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A premium fillet from a rare highland species, smoked slowly over hardwood until the flesh is dense and deeply aromatic. The smoke binds to the oils in a way that carries on water far longer than anything else, a scent that the creatures of these rivers cannot ignore."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389311_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "King's River Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389312_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388032_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388033_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An epic cut from the highland depths"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389312_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thick, prized fillet from one of the great river fish of the highlands. The flesh is dense and rich, but it is the bones that craftsmen seek, unusually resonant, they carry vibration in ways that conventional materials cannot match."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389312_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient River Slab"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389313_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388034_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388035_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A legendary slab from the old rivers"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389313_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive cut from a legendary river creature that has haunted the highland waters for generations. The flesh is dark and ancient-tasting, but it is the rendered fat that scholars argue over, it preserves whatever it coats, indefinitely."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389313_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Kingly Cut"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389314_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388036_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A mythic cut from the King of Rivers"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389314_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A slab of flesh from the King of Rivers itself. Dense and dark, it carries the weight of the river's history. The bones, when dried and shaped, resonate at a frequency that craftsmen claim is unlike anything else, as if the river itself still runs through them."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389314_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Frozen Strip"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389315_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388037_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388038_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A cold strip from icy northern waters"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389315_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thin strip from a fish pulled through ice into freezing air. The flesh is pale and delicate, but the cold it carries is stubborn, it doesn't leave the strip easily, even after preparation. Those who work with cold materials have found uses for that lingering chill."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389315_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Frost-Salted Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389316_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388039_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388040_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388041_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fillet preserved in mountain frost"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389316_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fillet from the cold northern waters, salted and packed in frost to preserve it. The preservation process does something unusual to the fibers; they become dense in a way that improves the action of tools worked alongside them. Northern craftsmen figured this out long before anyone else."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389316_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Glacial Cut"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389317_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388042_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388043_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388044_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rare cut from glacial depths"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389317_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A firm fillet from a rare arctic species. The cold locked into the flesh does not dissipate on its own, even after curing, it carries a chill that attracts cold-water creatures from distances that make no sense. Ice fishermen have used this for generations without ever questioning why."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389317_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Arctic Prime Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389318_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388045_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388046_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A prime cut from the deep arctic"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389318_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thick, prized fillet from the deep arctic fisheries. The cold has concentrated everything. The flavor, the density, the strange rigidity that sets in after curing. Materials worked with rendered arctic fat take on a hardness that standard tanning cannot achieve."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389318_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Permafrost Prime"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389319_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388047_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388048_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388062_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A legendary cut from the frozen deep"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389319_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive fillet from a legendary arctic creature. The flesh is dense and cold to the touch even after cooking, a cold that doesn't come from temperature but from something older. Armorers who work with it say the resulting material holds its shape under conditions that should destroy it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389319_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Leviathan Slab"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389320_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388049_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A mythic slab from the Ice Leviathan"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389320_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A slab torn from the Ice Leviathan. It radiates cold and leaves frost on whatever it touches. Weavers who have worked with thread treated in its rendered fat describe an elasticity that shouldn't be possible, it stretches without weakening, absorbs without breaking."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389320_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bog-Pickled Strip"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389321_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388050_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388051_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A strip preserved in swamp brine"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389321_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thin strip from a common swamp fish, pickled in bog water as tradition demands. Acquired taste. The murk does something to the flesh, it becomes pungent in a way that masks other scents entirely, which is occasionally useful."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389321_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Murk-Dried Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389322_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388052_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388053_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fillet dried in swamp air"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389322_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A fillet from the murky swamp shallows, dried slowly in the humid air. The smell is difficult. But the dense oils it leaves behind have a penetrating quality that craftsmen working in difficult conditions have long valued."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389322_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bog-Smoked Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389323_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388054_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388055_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388056_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rare fillet smoked over peat"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389323_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rare swamp fillet smoked slowly over peat and mangrove root. The process strips away the mud and leaves something that carries a dual nature, a dense, binding quality that craftsmen prize, and a deep, carrying scent that travels through water in ways that should not be possible."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389323_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Deep Mire Cut"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389324_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388057_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388058_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An epic cut from the swamp depths"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389324_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A thick cut from one of the swamp's great predators. The flesh is dark and oily, almost too rich. Both armorers and alchemists claim it as essential to their work, and both are right, for different reasons that neither fully understands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389324_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient Bog Slab"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389325_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388059_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388060_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388063_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A legendary slab from the ancient swamp"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389325_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive slab from a legendary swamp creature that has survived centuries in the dark water. The flesh smells of deep time. The rendered fat preserves whatever it touches with an almost unnatural permanence."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389325_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Abyssal Fillet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389326_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_RecipesTable_388061_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A mythic fillet from the Ancient of the Deep"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389326_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A slab of flesh from the Ancient of the Deep. It pulses faintly and leaves a dark, indelible stain on whatever it touches. Scholars of the deep waters have long prized this quality. Pressed against parchment, it leaves marks that no water, flame, or time can erase. What is written in that ink stays written."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389326_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp Fishing Totem"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389154_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Marks this area as a Swamp fishing biome."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389154_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Temperate Fishing Totem"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389152_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Marks this area as a Temperate fishing biome."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389152_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Cold Fishing Totem"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389153_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Marks this area as a Cold fishing biome."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389153_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Warm Fishing Totem"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389155_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Marks this area as a Warm fishing biome."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389155_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sand Dragon Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389156_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A legendary desert trophy. The Sand Dragon surfaces only at the break of dawn, and never for the unprepared."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389156_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Most exiles who fish the desert never see one. Most who see one never land it. Those who do rarely speak of it, not from modesty, but because the words do not exist yet. Pre-Hyborian tablets called it the First Swimmer. You called it caught. Both things are true."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389156_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "King of Rivers Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389157_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy of unmatched prestige. The King of Rivers appears only when the sun stands at its highest, and only for those who have earned it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389157_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "There is a tradition among river fishermen: when you finally land the King, you stop for the day. Not because you have caught everything worth catching, though arguably you have, but because nothing that follows will matter much. Hang it well. It belongs on a wall, not at the bottom of a pack."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389157_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ice Leviathan Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389158_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy from the frozen abyss. The Ice Leviathan surfaces only in the first moments of midnight, when the ice cracks and the water turns black."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389158_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The northern clans left offerings at the water's edge on the coldest nights. You brought a rod instead. They might have called that blasphemy. Looking at what you landed, they might also have called it effective. Mount it somewhere the cold can see it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389158_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient of the Deep Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389159_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy pulled from the oldest darkness. The Ancient of the Deep was here before the swamp had a name, before the land above the water had one either."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389159_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The swamp tribes do not name it. To name a thing is to claim power over it, and no one holds power over the Ancient. You caught one. Whether that makes you brave, reckless, or simply lucky depends on who you ask. The Ancient did not offer its opinion."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389159_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Arid Moonfish Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389160_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy from the desert night. The Arid Moonfish surfaces only when both moons are reflected in the water."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389160_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Desert monks kept vigil for years to document a single sighting. They wrote treatises about it. They developed entire schools of thought around whether the fish was real or mythic. You pulled one out of the water with a rod. Somewhere, a monk is very irritated about this."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389160_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Sand Moray Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389161_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy from the river shadows. The Sand Moray hunts by warmth, not sight, and it found you first."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389161_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Desert fishermen have one rule about the Sand Moray: never reach into a river at night. You chose to fish for one instead. The fact that you are here to hang this trophy suggests it went better than expected. The Sand Moray would disagree, but it is no longer in a position to."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389161_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Nocturnal Char Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389162_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy that belongs to the dark. The Nocturnal Char feeds only in total darkness, its scales absorb light, and the memory of catching it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389162_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "There is something about the Nocturnal Char that stays with an angler long after the catch. Not pride, exactly. Something quieter. Like the moment you realise the dark was watching you back, and you won anyway."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389162_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Whiskered King Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389163_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy of river legend. Generations tried and failed to land the Whiskered King. You did not."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389163_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "River villages have been passing down stories of this catfish for as long as anyone can remember. Stories of the one that got away, mostly. The grandfathers of grandfathers tried. The current generation had stopped trying. Yours will not be that kind of story."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389163_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Frozen Sturgeon Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389164_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy older than the kingdoms above it. The Frozen Sturgeon has outlasted every empire that ever tried to harvest it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389164_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A Frozen Sturgeon carries more history in its scales than most ruins. To catch one is to briefly hold something that has watched the rise and fall of things you will only ever read about. It did not hurry for any of them. It did not hurry for you either, but here you both are."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389164_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Abyssal Burbot Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389165_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy from the lightless deep. The Abyssal Burbot spent its entire existence certain that darkness was all there was."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389165_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It came up from the black with the slow confusion of something that has never once considered the surface might exist. It still seems uncertain about this arrangement. The wall it now decorates is probably the most light it has ever encountered. It does not appear grateful."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389165_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Putrid Piranha Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389166_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy from the rot. Where its desert cousin hunts the living, the Putrid Piranha serves the dead, and its bite carries disease."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389166_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp healers warn that a single bite will fester within hours and claim the limb within days. You managed to land the whole fish. That is either exceptional skill or exceptional luck, and the distinction matters considerably less than the result. Avoid touching the teeth when you hang it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389166_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Black Lamprey Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389167_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy of pure darkness. The Black Lamprey latches on and never lets go, except when you make it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389167_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Swamp shamans use it in bloodletting rituals, claiming it draws out corruption along with blood. Whether this is medicine or superstition depends on whether the patient survives. The survival rate is not discussed. You survived catching one, which puts you in select company."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389167_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ghost Fish Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389168_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy that should not exist. Northern shamans say the Ghost Fish is not a creature of the living world. It is a soul that forgot to leave the river."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389168_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Most exiles who see one drifting past their line at midnight pull the line out and go home. You pulled in the fish instead. The shamans have not yet decided whether you are very brave or deeply disrespectful of the dead. Given the result, possibly both."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389168_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Plague Serpent Trophy"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389169_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A trophy of wrongness. Even those who caught a Plague Serpent say the feeling of unease never entirely goes away."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389169_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "It is a creature changed by something older and fouler than the swamp itself. Exiles who have landed one and survived describe a sense of wrongness that does not fade for days. Some say it never entirely does. Mounting it on a wall means you will see it regularly. Whether that seems like a good idea is between you and your better judgment."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389169_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Tide-Scrap Chowder"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389327_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A poor catch made warm and useful."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389327_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Scraps of tide-caught fish are boiled down with rough herbs and whatever salt the cook could spare. It is not noble fare, but in the Exiled Lands a hot bowl can feel like mercy."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389327_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Prepared Fish Dish"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389327_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_Fishing_ItemTable_389328_FirstModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
