  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Magic"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012417_SecondModifier",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed by Ymir"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012417_ThirdModifier",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012433_ThirdModifier",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ymir's Swordbreaker"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012421_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "RecipesTable_Ymirs_Respite_770124215_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An ancient and highly-advanced gladius marked with the heraldry of a long-lost empire. "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012421_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Traditionally used as an offhand parrying weapon with its special centerline slit, it is equally as deadly as a sword weilded by the trained warrior. Short swords are prized in Hyborian cultures for their ability to thrust and stab in tight spaces where no longer weapon could ever be wielded. This weapon has been blessed by the frost giant god Ymir and has been known to break the skull as much as an opponent's sword! "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012421_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Scroll (Ymir's Consecrated Axes)"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012429_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A note scrawled on flimsy paper"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012429_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "While this schematic shares no characters or syntax with any language of the age, the detailed step-by-step illustrations are intelligible by accomplished crafters. "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012429_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EAA_Itemtable_5545224_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EAA_Itemtable_5545225_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The Aesir view bears as the forefather of man. Aesirian lore views the bear as a symbol of inner strength, wisdom and healing. In particular, the female bear is seen as compassionate family-driven and fiercely protective beast. While the male bear is primarily associated with strength. Their gods are even known to take on the shape of a bear when visiting the human world. Polar bears have their own unique meanings and attributes in Aesirian culture. Adapted to a cold environment and blending into their surroundings, they are adept hunters and can easily outrun and outswim humans. It is said that Ymir himself is accompanied by two great polar bear companions. Legend tells of the northern most Aesirian clans being able to raise young cubs into mighty followers able to crush the toughest of their enemies."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012433_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Beastly"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012433_SecondModifier",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Aesirian Hauberk"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012434_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A chestpiece crafted in ancient Aesrian style"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012434_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> “Then suddenly the borealis, the snow-clad hills and the blazing heavens reeled drunkenly to Conan’s sight; thousands of fire-balls burst with showers of sparks, and the sky itself became a titanic wheel which rained stars as it spun. Under his feet the snowy hills heaved up like a wave, and the Cimmerian crumpled into the snows to lie motionless.” </> - The Frost-Giant’s Daughter By Robert E. Howard. This chest armor is of ancient aesirian origin and bears an old script in archaic motifs only deciphered by the eldest of Aesir cheiftans.Traditionally, a tunic of chain mail worn as defensive armor, the hauberk is a formidable defense from any type of attack. This heavy armor piece is substantial in weight causing the wearer to sacrifice some mobility."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012434_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Heavy Armor"
   },
