     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Glacier-Bite"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "BA48036F493373C1E3AC02853D69ADFB",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "018F4DA747661510E1C1519DEED486F3",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Glacier-Shard"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DB992646435B3D699EA0179ED877A3EC",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "79218F1440348DF0EB30EEABFAE8D71A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Glacier-Rush"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "7C5DE2234ECAE3B7748D0DA993B29F52",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "877773ED4CE9B424EAC5DEA41FF20339",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Mitra grant that I do not fail of this mighty trust!</> - The Hour of the Dragon\r\n\r\nThis feast is consumed in the name of Mitra. Mitra, chief god of Hyboria! Mitra, the righteous, the father of justice, the enemy of Set! May this meal open a holy and eternal spring in the belly.  May man's heart know mercy. Mitra, guard us against the powers of darkness.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Corruption Resistance - After eating this feast, you slowly lose corruption for 20 minutes. Cannot stack with the secondary effects of other religious feasts.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "9E85CB0A4B6EB8D8A282678A1A6687C4",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "This infusion is mixed from ambrosia and the essence of a peacefully departed soul. Though far from the most potent healing treatment that has been devised, it is unwavering and has the unique property of lingering for a greater period of time while guarding the soul against the influence of corruption.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Slowly heals you and removes corruption over 2 min. Cannot be removed by any means. Cannot stack with other religious combat consumables. 3 min cooldown shared with other infusions.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DDCA8E384B2DC6782B5314B8B465153D",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Their ghastly feasts were considered a sacrifice to the scaly god.</> - The Hour of the Dragon\r\n\r\nThis feast is consumed in the name of Set. Set, the Old Serpent! Set. Archenemy Iblis! Set, who is known as Damballah in the Southern kingdoms, whose holy scales blind all with their bright darkness! Set is a jealous god and requires constant sacrifices from his chosen. This meal is devoured as an offering to the Lord of Snakes. May it grow a nest of serpents in the belly of the eater.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Cold-Blooded - After eating this feast, if you get too hot you automatically cool yourself down. Cannot stack with the secondary effects of other religious feasts.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "965369FB4242D35F53E889AAAE125ACB",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Set is not right, just strong. As will you be if you drink this most arrogant of enhancements.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Drinking this fully restores your health and grants you 60% bonus strength, agility, and follower damage for 1 minute. During that time all healing you receive is severely reduced. Cannot stack with other religious combat consumables. 3 min cooldown shared with other infusions.</>\r\n"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "843BF5C9406EAF53C50C23BF24F7BC3B",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The practice of inscribing sigils into weapons has been invented countless times by countless cultures. The exact symbols used vary across the world but their power is indisputable.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>This weapon modification isn't itself a source of magic damage; instead it amplifies the damage dealt by other magical effects from weapons, armor sets, or sorcery.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "87D967D987825733C31240C087825733",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ODO_ItemTable_Add_47210133_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ODO_ItemTable_Add_47210134_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ODO_ItemTable_Add_4729005_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ODO_ItemTable_Add_4729006_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>There were grisly feasts beneath the moon, across whose red disk a bat-like shadow incessantly swept.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nThis feast is consumed in the name of Yog. Yog, the Lorde of Empty Abodes! Yog, cousin of them that slither in the immaculate slime of the Elder Night! All good and fearing worshipers of Yog must dedicate themselves to the consumption of only meat. All the faithful of Yog must taste human flesh once a month, lest they become unclean until they again perform this communion of body and blood.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Dark Satiety - After eating this feast, for 20 minutes your food and water are maintained. Cannot stack with the secondary effects of other religious feasts.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "318D13EB4B663142651CC49AB74F24AA",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The rituals of Derketo are often mocked by outsiders who do not understand the pleasures and lusts of the goddess. This feast, however, typifies the food served at the revels and orgies of the goddess. No rich or fatty foods here, no. This meal is designed to titillate and preserve the participants, awakening the tingling warmth of the goddess inside them and giving them the stamina to proceed through the night. \r\n\r\nOnly untutored fools think that the men and women who laze around the gauzy temples of Derketo are recovering from a night of strong wine.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Debauchery - After eating this feast, for 20 minutes getting drunk also heals you out of combat. Cannot stack with the secondary effects of other religious feasts.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "2F3CE91A4F2060F8A20827BB5EE17AE1",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Tall and fair and blue-eyed. Their god is Ymir, the frost-giant, and each tribe has its own king. They are wayward and fierce. They fight all day and drink ale and roar their wild songs all night.</> - The Phoenix on the Sword\r\n\r\nThis feast is consumed in the name of Ymir. Ymir, the Frost Giant and father of all lesser giants! Ymir, Lord of Storm and War! May he grant the strength to fight all of the day and drink all of the night. May this meal grant a warrior the bravery to die in battle, earning a place in Ymir's hall in Valhalla to feast and revel until the end of days.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Longhall's Warmth - After eating this feast, for 20 minutes you'll warm yourself up if you get too cold. Cannot stack with the secondary effects of other religious feasts.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "D6FB2E0740D328306D396199FA38DBF9",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ironhide Plating"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "555266224FC9AEC642A67EB52644181C",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ODO_RecipesTable_Add_4729000_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "EoT_RecipesTable_Add_47270013_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Armor plates scarred by ferocious battle"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "8C68C6BA49E63E559A2FABAEA04C5FAD",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "F8C3CD92457E9CCA4C0821B8D1C7B09D",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Fashioned from the pelts of Jhebbal Sag's mightiest children and hardened through decades of the great hunt, these plates were blessed in a ritual that required constant chanting for three days and three nights while scribes engraved Mitra's deepest mysteries across them. When affixed to armor they offer ample physical protection and some protection from sorcery too."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "14AE111F418B95550C6CA4863AA190E0",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Orb of Desecration"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A0A4D0F243E22351B5CBBC82B7811BCB",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An orb filled with disgusting substances"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "0FA631B04FF401E8A660D88F417F8B9D",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An orb packed with temple refuse, rendered fat, and tar-black offerings scraped from altars better left unnamed. When it breaks, the filth spreads in a glistening slick that befouls the ground and turns every step into a lurching stumble.\r\n\r\n<LoreItalics>Desecration: Throwing this orb at a world object or site of religious significance summons an Invocation, an open-world event where waves of religious enemies can be defeated for increasing rewards based on difficulty.</>"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "A7FE75FA43BEC5EE3A3EECB2EECE9548",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Desecration"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "D6E9575B477CE9245452D8BE28953738",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
