  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics> They stopped short. Conan faced them, not a naked man roused mazed and unarmed out of deep sleep to be butchered like a sheep, but a barbarian wide-awake and at bay, partly armored, and with his long sword in his hand.</> - The Phoenix on the Sword\n\nThis curved sword is ancient in design and may well be the precursor to the designs found in Yamatai."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24214_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24220_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24217_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Conan stood in the moonlit silence, the dripping sword sagging in his hand, staring down at the remnants of his enemy. The red eyes glared up at him with awful life, then glazed and set - the great hands knotted spasmodically and stiffened. And the oldest race in the world was extinct.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\n\nThis curved sword is ancient in design and may well be the precursor to the designs found in Yamatai."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24219_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24222_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24216_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics> In an instant he was the center of a hurricane of stabbing spears and lashing clubs. But he moved in a blinding blur of steel. Spears bent on his armor or swished empty air, and his sword sang its death-song.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\n\nThis curved sword is ancient in design and may well be the precursor to the designs found in Yamatai."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24221_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24215_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24218_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24223_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "While surface details concealed within the sword's construction hint at enhanced functions lost to time, Voidforge weapons are still unmatched at their primary purpose - killing. Whichever realm is responsible for the creation of such weaponry is unknown, but the constellations hidden within the weapon's adornment are not of this world. \n\nIn contrast with the typical longsword, the katana is a curved weapon with a single outward facing blade edge meant for slashing instead of thrusting. "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_50580_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>That's what the black people of Kush call the Apples of Derketa. Derketa is the Queen of the Dead. Drink a little of that juice, or spill it on your flesh, and you'd be dead before you could tumble to the foot of this crag.</> - Red Nails\r\n\r\nDerketo was originally worshipped in Shem, but was quickly adopted in Stygia and the Black Kingdoms further south.\r\n\r\nThe dual nature of Derketo is death and fertility, and as such she is often paired with the most powerful deity of the kingdom she is associated with. Derketo is the consort of Set in Stygia, but the companion of Dagon in Zembabwei. In Kush she is Derketa, Queen of the Dead, and there, she walks alone.\r\n\r\nThis ceremonial armor is designed to awe and seduce in equal measure."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "73C792EB4B2EBF1BAFAD8B9589987C5F",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "E331DED64B9522B098B69EA5F27F7ED1",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "551329674ABB2147D3ED8A831D5C0EE5",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "6A38D7CE485A8E60E7BABDBE736B5E9C",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "98E45DA0451041F6B29088BA440141C3",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Balthus saw a lean figure of middle height, almost hidden in ostrich plumes set on a harness of leather and copper. From amidst the plumes peered a hideous and malevolent face. The plumes puzzled Balthus. He knew their source lay half the width of a world to the south. They fluttered and rustled evilly as the shaman leaped and cavorted.</> - Beyond the Black River\r\n\r\nThe worship of Jhebbal Sag has long been forgotten by the civilized Hyborians, but his priests in the Black Kingdoms and Pictish wilderness still spread his religion through fear and violence.\r\n\r\nA large part of this is the ceremonial garb that priests don for their rituals. Ornate headdresses decorated with ostrich feathers are common - even among the Picts who trade for feathers with Zingaran pirates who carry them up from the south.\r\n\r\nDespite offering no protection, the intimidation that comes from wearing such a headdress should not be underestimated."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "5165A9CD471D2D08E2F63E943DFD4656",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>These walls were hung with black velvet tapestries, and between the tapestries hung shields and crossed weapons of fantastic make.</> - The God in the Bowl\r\n\r\nAmong the rituals of the cult of Set, is the ability to render special properties into base metals. In particular, gold is much favored by the priests of Set to be used in the creation of these divine shields, which they claim will offer the blessings of Set.\r\n\r\nSome have pointed out that the process which hardens the gold darkens it almost to the color of bronze, and that the specialized priests who perform the process often move on quickly to new cities and villages. But not too loudly. That would be blasphemous."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "4B65A9354B17F9D7A95A06B73CB67F92",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>The glowing snow lay empty and bare; high above his head the witch-lights flashed and played in a frosty sky gone mad, and among the distant blue mountains there sounded a rolling thunder as of a gigantic war-chariot rushing behind steeds whose frantic hoofs struck lightning from the snows and echoes from the skies.</> - The Frost-Giant's Daughter\r\n\r\nThis headpiece marks one as devout to Ymir, Father of Giants, Lord of Storm and War."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "157F61F54E1F930DE7BEE2AB86887966",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>And in that instant she flung her arms toward the lights that glowed in the skies above her and cried out in a voice that rang in Conan's ears for ever after: 'Ymir! Oh, my father, save me!' </> - The Frost-Giant's Daughter\r\n\r\nThis frigid armor of adamantine strength marks one as devout to Ymir, Father of Giants, Lord of Storm and War."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "F693D369405B1F1D34BB489015D5F9B3",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>'Not so!' cried an older man, whose eyes were wild and weird. 'It was Atali, the daughter of Ymir, the frost-giant! To fields of the dead she comes, and shows herself to the dying... She lures men from stricken fields into the wastelands to be slain by her brothers, the ice-giants, who lay men's red hearts smoking on Ymir's board.'</> - The Frost-Giant's Daughter\r\n\r\nThese gauntlets of ice and steel mark one as devout to Ymir, Father of Giants, Lord of Storm and War."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "0F44D9E041526C48C25D51B548BAEE9A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>'Swear not so often by Ymir,' uneasily muttered a warrior, glancing at the distant mountains.</> - The Frost-Giant's Daughter\r\n\r\nThese leggings, of a material both frosty and otherworldly, mark one as devout to Ymir, Father of Giants, Lord of Storm and War."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "E67A1DC5476AB68FD38FE0B09022545F",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Better if steel and bowstring prevail without further aid from the arts, for the constant use of mighty spells sometimes sets forces in motion that might rock the universe.</> - The Hour of the Dragon\r\n\r\nA well-made arrow can be the difference between a hit and a miss.\r\n\r\nArrows can be equipped by dragging them over the bow in the inventory."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "1396F1BD469FAF34062D6F994FFBA39C",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>He wondered how many poor devils had been bludgeoned in their sleep and dragged out of that room and down the road that ran through the shadowed palm groves to the roasting pit.</>  - Shadows in Zamboula\r\n\r\nThis sinister weapon is made of the bones of a human arm bound to a large fragment of stone. \r\n\r\nCannibalism is more than a perverted appetite to the men of Darfar: it is an integral element of their cult. This cudgel is one of the ritual objects of the Yoggite religion. It is used to bludgeon human prey so that they can be carried to the sacrifice pit unblemished.\r\n\r\nBone is a brittle substance that breaks easily under even a small amount of force. Anything made of bone will fall apart quickly."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "75B31B714957F3A0545028B68B515989",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Black men came up the river in long boats with skulls grinning on the prows, or stole stooping through the trees, spear in hand.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nAdorned with feathers and tipped with flint, this short spear represents the pinnacle of Darfari weapons.\r\n\r\nThe Darfari use these spears for hunting game, first pinning their prey with well-aimed throws and then harassing their prey with swift, sharp stabs.\r\n\r\nThe feathers on the shaft are taken from the ferocious, but colourful, elephant birds that roam the grasslands on the very edges of Darfar."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "D7DDC14D49EC10E2AFD0668865C661A0",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>It was like a big black jade bead, such as the temple girls of Yezud wear when they dance before the black stone spider which is their god. Yar Afzal held it in his hand, and he did not pick up anything else. Yet when he fell dead, a spider, like the god at Yezud, only smaller, ran out of his fingers.</> - The People of the Black Circle\r\n\r\nThe temple dancers of Yezud are famous for their cavorting in front of the idol of their spider god. Naked but for strings of beads in webbed patterns, the dancers are all virgins, set to serve in the temple for five years.\r\n\r\nRumor has it that the temple dancers are less chaste than the priests would have their congregations believe - and that the priests instead use the dancers for their own pleasure.\r\n\r\nWhether there is any truth to the rumors, many of the male temple dancers stay on at the temple to become priests, while the girls, once done with their service, are given a generous dowry to help them find a suitor."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "E417C1B94F55EA9C90DCB4B87ECE568A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Rainbow-hued were the vestments of the other priests. One wore a scarlet gown and azure headgear; another a purple robe topped by a saffron turban; and yet another a gown of sapphire blue surmounted by a headdress of pale celadon.</> - Conan and the Spider God - de Camp, L. Sprague\r\n\r\nThe temple dancers of Yezud are famous for their cavorting in front of the idol of their spider god. Naked but for strings of beads in webbed patterns, the dancers are all virgins, set to serve in the temple for five years.\r\n\r\nRumor has it that the temple dancers are less chaste than the priests would have their congregations believe - and that the priests instead use the dancers for their own pleasure.\r\nWhether there is any truth to the rumors, many of the male temple dancers stay on at the temple to become priests, while the girls, once done with their service, are given a generous dowry to help them find a suitor."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "70EA460A4B7F240C1452B5B9707E76B1",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "9FFEE2D840B310D16FCFE3BE926B7C45",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "641DA4FA4699A5B17F59CEB0AA090D14",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "AEF6366E4657FAD0421F91896810373A",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>A long bow and a strong bow, and let the sky grow dark! The cord to the nock, the shaft to the ear, and the king of Koth for a mark!</> - Song of the Bossonian Archers.\r\n\r\nCarved from a single piece of wood, the hunting bow is used across the world and in hundreds of variants.\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle.\r\n\r\nThis bow will be able to bring down both human and non-human foes, but it relies heavily on the skill of the wielder."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "AB99A3C54802E5F37D87E88095E38112",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "8373E1B142F6CFF30172448590654473",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "8AE199AF4160D05D79789FB849A0FF61",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "19DE8FF84B669173D3682180D360705A",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "B930B0D1438FED3DA674E498EE20E61D",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "2B47B4744721038EAADC8C9CE39B9C8E",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "15BF75064123B3BF51AC398E4DF36A4C",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "E6DCA9C44D75FC82B76DBCBF1C5AEE89",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "8135EB9A4C73233C619CCCA3381C66AA",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "0A2750AC459783D5A01967A5271DBC02",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "9146F25640FC26E80A3BBA9E15157C9D",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Kerim Shah had unslung the powerful Turanian bow that killed at five hundred paces, and the Irakzai looked to their own lighter and less lethal bows.</> - The People of the Black Circle\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "B2BD6A774EEC6A438F1C7EA196505251",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "C265AF3543B04FB652AD18B51992A6B2",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DB8A491D41201D9EF86C52A0EB60DE39",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics> Kerim Shah had unslung the powerful Turanian bow that killed at five hundred paces, and the Irakzai looked to their own lighter and less lethal bows.</> - The People of the Black Circle\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "5492A86D44DE5EBA2695379B95301217",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DAFA12A94887BFC73395959E95D6C68D",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "858F8264461F280919A582BBDAD08D19",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Instinctively Conan loosened the great sword in its sheath. The pyramid on which he rested was four-sided, one - the side toward the jungle - carved in broad steps. In his hand was a Shemite bow, such as Belit had taught her pirates to use. A heap of arrows lay at his feet, feathered ends towards him, as he rested on one knee.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nCarved from a single piece of wood, the hunting bow is used across the world and in hundreds of variants.\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle.\r\n\r\nThis bow will be able to bring down both human and non-human foes, but it relies heavily on the skill of the wielder."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "015A278D47B9AB7AC47762911561B563",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Instinctively Conan loosened the great sword in its sheath. The pyramid on which he rested was four-sided, one - the side toward the jungle - carved in broad steps. In his hand was a Shemite bow, such as B?lit had taught her pirates to use. A heap of arrows lay at his feet, feathered ends towards him, as he rested on one knee.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nCarved from a single piece of wood, the hunting bow is used across the world and in hundreds of variants.\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle.\r\n\r\nThis bow will be able to bring down both human and non-human foes, but it relies heavily on the skill of the wielder."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "608447DD4A701992AF5711B00C45BC13",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "55A85CCC4624D064891E98BF74570A98",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "A9612549495DE4477D9B09821765FD40",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "92FA838A4AC07EA1E532848FD6761A8D",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Kerim Shah had unslung the powerful Turanian bow that killed at five hundred paces, and the Irakzai looked to their own lighter and less lethal bows.</> - The People of the Black Circle\r\n\r\nThis bow is made in the Hyrkanian style, using different materials to strengthen different areas of the bow and allowing it to be shorter than a longbow. For Hyrkanians, who spend most of their lives shooting from horseback, this is a necessity.\r\n\r\nHyrkanians are widely considered the best archers in the world, raised to the hunt and the art of shooting from horseback. Their bows, however, are not as well made as those of the Shemites, who have spent centuries perfecting the art.\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "72579736479A85B7911423BF18125AF1",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "3711FA314A7C477F2748B494D87B55D2",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Springing to his feet, he bent his bow powerfully and drove his last shaft point blank at a great hairy shape that soared up at his throat. The arrow was a flying beam of moonlight that flashed onward with but a blur in its course, but the were-beast plunged convulsively in midair and crashed headlong, shot through and through.</> - Queen of the Black Coast\r\n\r\nCreated based on an ancient design found in the Exiled Lands, this bow seems to confuse the eye with its odd, alien curves.\r\n\r\nIn the thrum of the bowstring, it whispers of gibbering terrors screeching beneath a blood-red moon and the terrified screams of those who flee the merciless hunt.\r\n\r\nOne who holds this bow too long risks being drawn into its miasma of madness."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "99255A3A49C8ED42932D9D9DD3D60B4F",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>A long bow and a strong bow, and let the sky grow dark! The cord to the nock, the shaft to the ear, and the king of Koth for a mark!</>\r\nSong of the Bossonian Archers.\r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle.\r\n\r\nThis bow will be able to bring down both human and non-human foes, but it relies heavily on the skill of the wielder.\r\n"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "55BCA49947B57D11E94384A7EDC693E4",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "8F19FC5F4496960B547AEE831CB62BB2",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "AFD5BE5E47BB1C98566D67BCBCB16B47",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>And their magicians made a terrible magic to guard the city; for by their necromantic arts they re-created the dragons which had once dwelt in this lost land, and whose monstrous bones they found in the forest. Those bones they clothed in flesh and life, and the living beasts walked the earth as they walked it when time was young.</> - Red Nails\r\n\r\nThrough the long passage of eons, rumors of dragons have always been passed down from generation to generation, and the legacy of these fearsome creatures grows with each telling."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "E961FBDD45C57A32F1C95E8853231DA6",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Its composition was something like copper, but much harder, and it was carved with hieroglyphics, like those found on the more ancient menhirs in southern Stygia.</> - The God in the Bowl\r\n\r\nHistorians link the rise and eventual fall of the Khari empire to its dominion over the slave trade. In fact, it's believed the Khari gained their reputation as master crafters through the careful theft and assimilation of knowledge held by those they enslaved.\r\n\r\nWhen the inevitable occurred and slave turned against master, Khari survivors fled west to the desert where they encountered the last remaining vestiges of the serpent people. As devout worshippers of Set, the Khari venerated the serpent folk as living scions of their beloved reptile God and laid the foundations for the kingdom that would later be known as Stygia. What finally befell the Khari and their scaled patrons is lost to time. \r\n\r\nIn trained hands, bows are lethal weapons that can bring down a foe from afar. A large part of the versatility of the bow comes from the arrows used in battle."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "F1118F0146EE07428D09D19289A0960A",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "A14EBD0140031C6B851354AF8E215EC9",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>Balthus saw a lean figure of middle height, almost hidden in ostrich plumes set on a harness of leather and copper. From amidst the plumes peered a hideous and malevolent face. The plumes puzzled Balthus. He knew their source lay half the width of a world to the south. They fluttered and rustled evilly as the shaman leaped and cavorted.</> - Beyond the Black River\r\n\r\nThe worship of Jhebbal Sag has long been forgotten by the civilized Hyborians, but his priests in the Black Kingdoms and Pictish wilderness still spread his religion through fear and violence.\r\n\r\nA large part of this is the ceremonial garb that priests don for their rituals. Garments sewn from the skins of their prey drape the bodies of those that truly relish the hunt."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "9AC81EED48B75F0B867A0A8BB011168C",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "A6E3C003426638CFCEAD969E20D3FA86",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "8764507946C5DD60A66148BD251CAA87",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
