  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A mask worn by devotees of Set"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952501_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952501_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The dispassionate features of the serpent have been modeled and refined in this mask. It distorts the features of the wearer and brings them closer to the cold beauty of the serpents so beloved of their god.\nUsed primarily in rituals within the temple of Set, this mask nevertheless offers a certain level of protection for the face of the wearer."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952501_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Umbral Setite Choker"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952502_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952502_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A choker worn by devotees of Set"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952502_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952502_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Crafted from the finest golds, this garment is light and supple. It molds pleasingly to the form and accentuates the chest. The mysteries of Set are not all blood and death - the ritual that depicts the coupling of Set with his mistress, Derketo, has been described by Mitrean scholars as \"a blasphemous orgy of wine and blood.\" Though they always take the opportunity to vist any temple of Derketo during such rites. For the purposes of research, of course."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952502_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Umbral Setite Shendyt"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952504_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952504_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A shendyt worn by devotees of Set"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952504_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952504_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Woven silk edged with golden trim has been used to shape this ornamental shendyt. Worn by devotees of Set during their rituals, these shendyts are often stained in the blood of sacrifice."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952504_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Umbral Setite Sandals"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952505_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952505_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A pair of sandals worn by devotees of Set"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952505_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousRecipeTable_6952505_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "These ceremonial sandals were not designed for the harsh environment of the desert, but rather the stone floors of the temple. Runnng in sand wearing these is an uncomfortable experience and fighting in them is almost impossible due to poor balance."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "LegitReligiousItemTable_6952505_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
