    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Dark Crystal"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790349_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Black transparent, shimmering stone"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790349_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Brittle, impossible to work with conventional tools, crystal is mostly used for focusing light and creating rudimentary lenses.\nThe Black Seers of Mount Yimsha craft great lenses to aid in their astrological divinations. Black sorceries gain potency when the heavens are in certain configurations."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790349_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Dark Mortar"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790345_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "This cold, hard artificial lava is of no further interest, unless heated in an Ancient Furnace"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790345_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The Exiled Lands stand as a testament to the efficacy of weather at destroying the works of man. When the wind howls across the landscape and the sand scours everything in its path, there are few buildings that survive for very long.\nHowever, the supernaturally large insects of the Exiled Lands have developed a natural secretion that helps to protect them against the environment. \nIchor from these creatures, when soaked into twine and bound to a stone surface, can be placed into a furnace and hardened into bricks that provide excellent protection against the rigors of the Exiled Lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790345_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790350_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Molten Mortar"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790350_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790350_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790250_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A true artificial lava, this mixture must still be molten to strengthen the Darkstone and obtain the famous Ancient Stone"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790350_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ancient Stone"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790347_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790347_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Chunk of dark stone obtained by burning stone using dark powder as fuel"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790347_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790347_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Dark Wood"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790344_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790344_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Wood treated with resin"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790344_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Wood is an abundant source of fuel and building material.\nReadily available and easily shaped with the right tools, wood is ubiquitous in the weapons and buildings of primitive tribes and mighty nations.\n\nWood allows for the creation of fire and its easy transport.\n\nThis wood has been treated with resin, making it stronger and more weather resistant."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790344_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Calcined Iron Bar"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790342_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790342_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Iron ingot burnt and oxidized by black powder"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790342_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_RecipesTable3790342_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The ability to work iron is a step along the road from savagery to civilization. The streets of the great cities of the world resound with the ring of hammer on anvil a song to the march of progress.\nIron weapons and armor offer superior protection, but the additional weight means carrying less supplies.\nIron can be treated with Steelfire in a Furnace to produce steel."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Ancient_Civ_ItemTable3790342_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
