    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Derketo's Kiss"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51456_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A tool for extracting unfulfilled desires"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51456_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51462_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Derketo teaches that when a person dies their unfulfilled desires manifest within their bodies. The worshippers of Derketo have created this tool for extracting that...remnant from those who die while under their ministrations.\n\nJust don't look too closely at what it pulls out."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51456_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51462_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Derketo's Kiss"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51462_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Hoar-Frost Hatchet"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51460_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blood Letter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51455_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A tool for extracting the blood of victims"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51455_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51461_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "When Jhebbal Sag visits this realm, he chooses a form and enters his sacred groves. Occasionally, he will mate with the female of a species and create a divine child.\nThrough generations of breeding, many creatures contain some trace of the divine blood of Jhebbal Sag. \n\nThe blood letter can be used to harvest the blood of victims, which can be used in the sacrifice rituals of Jhebbal Sag."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51455_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51461_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Blood Letter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51461_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Mitraen Ankh"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51304_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An Ankh used in the ritual purification of the dead"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51304_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51457_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">'Mitra would have folks stand upright before him - not crawling on their bellies like worms, or spilling blood of animals all over his altars.'</> - Black Colossus\n\nThe purification of the dead is considered an important part of the death rites of Mitra. When one dies, the vessel that was the body is usually consigned to the flames in a rite that was borne from the legend of the phoenix. It is said that in cleasning the body with fire, a new soul can be reborn from the ashes.\n\nHowever, before a body is burned, it is ritually purified using an Ankh of Mitra. The body is struck with the Ankh to push out any trace of spirit left trapped within the body, preventing the corpse from rising again and sealing it against necromancy."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51304_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51457_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Mitraen Ankh"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51457_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Setite Ritual Knife"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51459_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A formal dagger used for ritualistic killings"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51459_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51902_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> She has instituted human sacrifice, and since her mating with Constantius, no less then five hundred men, women and children have been immolated. Some of these have died on the altar she has set up in the temple, herself wielding the sacrificial dagger, but most have met a more horrible doom. </> - A Witch Shall be Born\n\nThe devotees of Set are spread far and wide in the lands of Stygia and the Old Serpent demands human sacrifice as a part of his worship.\n\nThese daggers are crafted in the thousands at the forges of Luxur and then spread to the priesthood of the Serpent god.\n\nWhile the rituals of Set are many and depraved, the fastest is bending a victim over an altar and cutting their heart from their chest."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51459_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51902_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Setite Ritual Knife"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51902_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Yog Cleaver"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51458_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A rudimentary axe created from a jawbone bound to a stout branch"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51458_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51854_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> On the heels of the shout came a clamor of blood-freezing screams, the shattering impact of axes on the gate.</> - The Black Stranger\n\nBladed weapons are generally frowned upon by the worshippers of Yog, but this jawbone is dull enough that it acts more like a club than a sword.\nYoggites believe that the consumption of human flesh gives them the Blessing of Yog for a period of time, which grants them invulnerability to normal weapons.\n\nWhile Yog is considered a deity in Darfar, scholars in Hyboria classify him as a demon of the Elder night, referencing ancient documents that survived the drowning of Atlantis."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51458_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51854_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Yog Cleaver"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51854_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zathite Ritual Dagger"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51908_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A venom-tipped dagger used in Zathite rituals"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51908_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51909_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zath is a god who speaks of purity to his cult, predicting that he will one day arise and sweep across the land, cleansing it of decadence. His cultists work to spread his work and works throughout the kingdom of Zamoria.\n\nCarried by Exiles to the Exiled Lands and the Isle of Siptah, the teachings of the god have found followers among those who feel abandoned by their regular gods.\n\nThe primary means of execution for those who disobey the commandments of Zath is to put them in the tunnels beneath the great temple in Yezud and allow the to be devoured by Zath and his children. This is a ritual of purification and the dead are considered blessed by Zath. Their corpses are burned in the eternal flame of the temple as an offering to Zath.\n\nFor those who are far from Yezud, this dagger tipped in venom will have to take the place of a venomous spider."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51908_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51909_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Blessed Zathite Ritual Dagger"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_EmberReligiousToolsTweaks_51909_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Growing in the cold of the highlands, these berries are used in the making of juice and wine. They can be eaten, though they do not offer much nourishment. Still, any sustenance is good sustenance when waiting for meatier prey."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_HortiMergeItems_18005_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Growing in the dry wastes of the desert, these berries are used in the making of juice and wine. They can be eaten, though they do not offer much nourishment. Still, any sustenance is precious out in the desolate lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "DT_HortiMergeItems_18006_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Crude Planter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18520_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A crude planter for slowly growing plants"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18520_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "When man discovered the secrets of agriculture, the world changed. No longer roving bands of battling tribes, the first villages and cities formed around the idea that going out hunting food was a lot harder than just growing it safely behind walls.\n\nThis planter is very crude, and seeds sown in it will grow slowly."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18520_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Planter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18521_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A planter for growing plants"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18521_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "When man discovered the secrets of agriculture, the world changed. No longer roving bands of battling tribes, the first villages and cities formed around the idea that going out hunting food was a lot harder than just growing it safely behind walls.\n\nThis planter is a standard design, and seeds sown in it will grow at a regular rate."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18521_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Improved Planter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18522_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An improved planter for quickly growing plants"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18522_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "When man discovered the secrets of agriculture, the world changed. No longer roving bands of battling tribes, the first villages and cities formed around the idea that going out hunting food was a lot harder than just growing it safely behind walls.\n\nSowing seeds in this planter will cause them to grow quickly over time."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18522_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Compost Heap"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18519_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A smelly pile of rotting matter"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18519_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "dt_Horti_ItemTableRow_5100001_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "dt_Horti_recipetablerow_5100004_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Ask not a man what goes into his compost heap. That is his business alone. It is what a man removes from his compost heap that matters."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18519_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
