     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Somewhere, far from the Exiled Lands, a scholar sits writing frantically. His master has given him the task of writing hundreds of descriptions of mundane items, from swords and armor, to plant fiber and stones. He glances at the next item on his list. Ladder. \n\nHe stops, sets his quill down and looks at his reflection in a nearby mirror. He is a man grown old before his time, a slave in all but name to his masters. \n\n'What am I doing', he wonders. His life is a series of decisions that he almost didn't recognize that he was making.  As his thoughts spiral into the past and as he traces that inevitable trajectory backwards he realizes that there was no single point, no decision that brought him to this point. It was an accumulation of decisions across his entire lifespan, building around him like sand in the desert that leaves him living a life of quiet desperation, drowning slowly as the quicksand fills his throat.\n\nAs the realization hits him, he feels a vast sadness, an aching in his soul that he could have been so much more than simply this. A single, crystalline tear seeps from his eye and drips down onto the parchment he is working on, blurring the ink.\n\nResolving to make more of this life, the man stands, pushing aside his parchment, and moving to the door.\n\nWhich bursts open and, before the surprised scribe can even gasp, he is run through by a wild-eyed thief who has crept into the mansion in search of valuables.\n\nThe thief wipes his knife on the dead scholar's clothing, and glances around the room. His gaze wanders across the parchment on the table, filled with a list of items and descriptions written in the neat hand of the deceased scholar. He grins, and reaches for the quill.\n\nLater, when the guards find the dead scholar, lying facefirst in a mingled pool of blood and ink, they will be briefly distracted by the bizarre message scratched into the parchment beside the word ladder. It simply reads: \"Something you climb, idiot\".\n\nThe guards shrug. Nobody really cares about the text anyway."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210162_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A well that fills slowly over time"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210163_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "RecipesTable_80131_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A saddle designed for traveling distances with extra storage space"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210165_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The Exiled Lands has no tradition in riding. The terrain is downright unfriendly to horses and the beasts themselves have no natural presence here. However, due to sheer-minded persistence and strong will, horses have been tamed and brought to the Exiled Lands. A testament and a congratulations to all who suffered to make this happen.\n\nSome types of cavalry rely on their speed and mobility to perform flanking Maneuvers, while others are all about the charge. This saddle is designed for the latter - allowing attackers to stay in the stirrups taking repeated blows while they use the momentum of their mounts to force a break in enemy lines. For anyone who wishes to ride a mount into battle and stay there for a while, this is the saddle of choice."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210165_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Improved Tanner's Table"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210166_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210166_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The tanner's table is where processed hides are assembled into a finished product."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210166_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210166_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_18544_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">The rest were toilers, without armor save for shirts of toughened leather, but they were brawny stalwarts, and skilled in the use of their hunting bows...</> - The Black Stranger\n\nSimply put, the tanner's table is where cured animal skins are transformed into useable products including shoes, belts, and scabbards or further treated, layered, and hardened as part of the armourcraft process. The tanner's table includes all manner of sewing, cutting, and leather-punching tools."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210166_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Improved Artisan Table"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210167_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210167_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Set"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210168_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210168_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A shrine to Set, the Old Serpent"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210168_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">Ships did not put unasked into this port, where dusky sorcerers wove awful spells in the murk of sacrificial smoke mounting eternally from blood-stained altars where naked women screamed, and where Set, the Old Serpent, arch-demon of the Hyborians but god of the Stygians, was said to writhe his shining coils among his worshippers.</> - The Hour of the Dragon\n\nCreated as a focal point for the worship of Set, this pristine shrine will not remain so for long. \n\nThe hunger of Set requires human sacrifice and the altars of Set regularly run with blood.\n\nAltars can also be used to perform rituals of creation - placing certain items on the altar can invoke the blessings of the gods."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210168_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Mitra"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210169_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210169_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Considered a good god, Mitra is worshipped throughout the Hyborian kings, replacing the worship of Bori from which those primitive tribes took their name.\n\nMitra's symbol is that of the phoenix, but when he is depicted it is in the form of a well built, bearded man. He abhors the bloody rituals of other religions and prefers for his followers to perform dignified, purification rituals.\n\nMitra's priests preach a monotheistic doctrine and as such their followers tend to persecute the members of other nearby religions. Due to this tendency, Chapels to Mitra cannot be built within a very long range of shrines to other gods."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210169_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Yog"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210170_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210170_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">Somewhere near by had been the pit, dark and awful, wherein screaming victims were fed to a nameless amorphic monstrosity which came up out of a deeper, more hellish cavern.</> - Black Colossus\n\nThe altars of Yog are crude sacrifice pits, lined with spikes and stones. Victims are hauled up to a rough stone platform and then uncerimonously booted into the pit. \n\nWhen the victim has finished shrieking, the worshippers of Yog gather and partake of the purified flesh.\n\nIt is said that the blessing of Yog falls upon anything within the pit. It is not uncommon to meet Yoggites who have smeared themselves with ashes from their sacrifice pits and decorated themselves with the bones of their victims."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210170_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Ymir"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210171_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210171_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">The clangor of the swords had died away, the shouting of the slaughter was hushed; silence lay on the red-stained snow. The bleak pale sun that glittered so blindingly from the ice-fields and the snow-covered plains struck sheens of silver from rent corselet and broken blade, where the dead lay as they had fallen. The nerveless hand yet gripped the broken hilt; helmeted heads back-drawn in the death-throes, tilted red beards and golden beards grimly upward, as if in last invocation to Ymir the frost-giant, god of a warrior-race...</> - The Frost-Giant's Daughter\n\nIt is said that the battlefield is truly Ymir's altar. The war god does not want murdered sacrifices so much as beautiful deaths during the din of glorious combat. Yet those most devoted to the Lord of Storm and War still find themselves constructing places where they can directly commune with their god through the medium of spilt blood. On the cold winds of deadly winter, one might hear the grinding whisper of the Father of Giants saying, 'You get what you give.'"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210171_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Jhebbal Sag"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210172_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210172_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Though the Lord of Beasts prefers natural locations for his sacred groves, it is understood that men no longer live in the deep wilds of the world. Thus, the altars of Jhebbal Sag tend to be built of crude stone and hacked into a basic likeness. Too much polish would be reminiscent of man without the component of the beast. Too little polish would alienate mankind.\n\nThough Jhebbal Sag rarely visits such altars, he will receive sacrifices made here and eventually provide the power to manifest his avatar."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210172_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Zath"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210173_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210173_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A crude altar to Zath"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210173_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Zath's cult represent him as a deity of purity and cleansing. That he will one day arise and cleanse the decadent world of wicked men and their sins.\n\nThis altar to Zath is little more than a hole in the ground. Zath teaches that to purify the hearts of men, the way must be opened for the spiders of the earth. This is an attempt to create a space where those spiders can flourish."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210173_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Shrine to Derketo"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210174_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210174_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Derketo is a fertility goddess and she is worshipped for her ability to grant bounteous crops and good calving seasons. Her rituals, however, involved deviant orgies that can last for weeks and include necrophilia and bestiality.\n\nHer places of worship are therefore chosen for comfort, style, and the freeing of inhibitions. They are places where life and death intertwine like a pair of lovers. Those who visit the pleasure places of Derketo are reminded what it is to live and die - and how pleasurable both can be."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210174_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Frying Pan"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210175_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A cast Iron Frying Pan for searing meats on a stovetop"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210175_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "a flat-bottomed pan used for frying, searing, and browning foods. It is typically 20 to 30 cm (8 to 12 in) in diameter with relatively low sides that flare outwards, a long handle, and no lid. Larger pans may have a small grab handle opposite the main handle. "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210175_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Alcohol Distiller"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210176_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210176_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Alchemical equipment repurposed for a greater more glorious purpose "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210176_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210176_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A still is an apparatus used to distill liquid mixtures by heating to selectively boil and then cooling to condense the vapor. A still uses the same concepts as a basic distillation apparatus, but on a much larger scale. Stills are used to produce distilled beverages containing ethanol."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210176_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Scrawled Note"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210177_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Hand scrawled note "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210177_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Use to see what they are about"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210177_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Rolled Map"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210178_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A Map "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210178_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Use to see for where"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210178_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210179_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Map Frame"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210179_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A Framed Map "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210179_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Powder Bin"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210205_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Tavern Bar"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210217_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A Bar with a counter for serving guests, and cabinets for storage"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210217_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210217_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The counter at which drinks are served by a bartender is called \"the bar\". This term is applied, as a synecdoche, to drinking establishments called \"bars\". This counter typically stores a variety of beers, wines, liquors, and non-alcoholic ingredients, and is organized to facilitate the bartender's work."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210217_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210218_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210219_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210220_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bar Counter, Large"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210218_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bar Counter, Corner"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210219_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Bar Counter, Small"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210220_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Entertainer's Lute"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210221_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210130_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A delicate instrument in a world of savagery. The lute brings melodies to soothe the soul."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210221_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210130_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Resting on the stage, this well-worn lute awaits the hands of a skilled entertainer thrall. Its carved wood and taut strings echo with the melodies of faraway lands and forgotten times. When played, its soothing or spirited tunes can lift morale and charm even the fiercest of warriors."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210221_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Entertainer's Fiddle"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210222_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210131_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "An instrument of both joy and sorrow, the fiddle's high-pitched tunes cut through the silence of the wilderness."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210222_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210131_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Set upon the stage, this finely crafted fiddle is ready to sing under the touch of a skilled thrall. Its strings hum with the potential for vibrant jigs or mournful ballads. Whether in the halls of kings or by the campfires of the exiled, the music of this fiddle can captivate and inspire all who hear it."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210222_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Entertainer's Horn"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210223_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210132_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A horn unleashes deep, resonant tones that carry across the Exiled Lands. "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210223_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210132_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Resting prominently on the stage, this horn waits for the breath of a skilled entertainer thrall to unleash its mighty sound. Carved from the tusk of a great beast, its thunderous tones can rouse warriors to battle or signal victory in grand feasts. A single blast from this instrument commands respect across the Exiled Lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210223_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Entertainer's Song"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210224_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210133_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "When performed by a skilled entertainer, a song can enchant listeners, recounting tales of forgotten heroes, tragic love, or triumphant conquests."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210224_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210133_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The spot where a skilled entertainer thrall can sing. From ballads of lost kingdoms to war chants that inspire armies, the stand amplifies their voice, filling halls or battlefields with songs that stir emotions and strengthen resolve in the Exiled Lands."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210224_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Tavern Serving Station"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210225_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "Core_Recipes_210225_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A tavern is a type of business where people gather to drink alcoholic beverages and be served food such as different types of roast meats and cheese, and where travelers could receive lodging."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "Core_ItemTable_210225_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
