  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the display, cultivation and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "dt_Horti_ItemTableRow_5102154_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "dt_Horti_ItemTableRow_5102155_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Some gardens are for ornamental purposes only, while some gardens also produce food crops, sometimes in separate areas, or sometimes intermixed with the ornamental plants. Food-producing gardens are distinguished from farms by their smaller scale, more labor-intensive methods, and their purpose (enjoyment of a hobby rather than produce for sale). Flower gardens combine plants of different heights, colors, textures, and fragrances to create interest and delight the senses."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "dt_Horti_ItemTableRow_5102154_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "dt_Horti_ItemTableRow_5102155_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
