  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Xhal'Zurith Ultra Greatsword"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492243_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_RecipeTable_New_2491715_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive two handed sword imbued with Empowering Afflictions & Decaying Strikes"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492243_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_RecipeTable_New_2491715_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Xhal’zurith is not a weapon forged  it is a relic torn from the bones of annihilation itself. Its blade is jagged, torn, and unnatural, like a malformed fang broken from the jaw of something vast and hateful. The edges do not cut, they rip. The core of the blade appears hollowed and blackened, pulsing with a viscous, shadow-like energy that seeps and stains whatever it touches.It is said Xhal’zurith was ripped from the corpse of a devouring god, buried deep beneath the charred earth at the end of the last age. When the sky cracked and the mountains wept blood, it rose carried not by a hero, but by a butcher with no name, who carved his path through kings and monsters alike until the weapon consumed him, body and soul.The sword hums with an unsettling vibration, as if straining against its own bindings, always wanting more. Wielders report hearing whispers, not in words, but in raw sensation: rage, emptiness, hunger. Xhal’zurith does not simply kill, it devours essence, leaving husks where warriors once stood. Armor corrodes. Magic falters. Courage dies.To carry it is to suffer its bite. Over time, the user’s flesh cracks, darkens, becomes alien. Some mutate. Some vanish. But all are erased, eventually, as if Xhal’zurith unmakes those who dare to hold it.Despite this, there are always those who reach for it. Power draws fools as blood draws flies. And Xhal’zurith waits. Commissioned by Toni."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492243_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Vargmir Ultra Greatsword"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492244_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_RecipeTable_New_2491716_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A massive two handed sword imbued with Healing Attacks & Lacerating Strikes"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492244_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492289_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_RecipeTable_New_2491716_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_RecipeTable_New_2491731_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "\"Not forged — hewn from the frozen corpse of something ancient. It does not shine. It hungers.\"A blade not born of mortal hands, Vargmir, the Cold Devourer is a jagged greatsword carved from blackened glacial stone, shot through with veins of hoarfrost that never melt. Heavy and raw, its weight speaks of ancient violence, and its edge though chipped and uneve bites with a primal finality. The surface is coarse like permafrost, lined with spidery fractures that pulse faintly with a cold, pale glow, as if something long-dead still stirs within.Vargmir is no elegant weapon; it is a beast’s tooth, torn from the maw of a forgotten titan felled in the north, where even time dares not tread. It hums with a low, animal growl when drawn subtle at first, then louder, deeper, the longer it tastes the air. Some say it is alive. Others say it remembers. And what it remembers, it wants to destroy.The blade drinks warmth. Metal around it grows brittle. Flame flees from it. Those struck by Vargmir often do not bleed, but freeze from the inside, their last breath caught in a rattle of frost. The wound it leaves is more than physical it is a curse of cold, a hunger that gnaws at the soul. Wielding it too long is to invite the cold into yourself, to feel your heart slow, your memories dim, your fury harden like ice.Once, it was wielded by a warlord known only as The Winter Maw, a pale giant who razed southern kingdoms with it, until even his own blood turned to ice and he crumbled into frozen dust. Since then, the sword has resurfaced only in times of great violenc as if drawn to battle, or seeking it.Its true nature remains a mystery, but one thing is certain: Vargmir does not serve. It chooses. Commissioned by Toni."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTable_2492244_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
