   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_51009_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "While this finely crafted implement functions as an ostentatious display of good fortune, its utility as a tool or weapon is questionable at best."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_51009_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Thrashing Maul"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24107_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24251_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">Before his coming they had filched steel weapons and armor from the Bossonians and Zingarans, or had hammered out their own crude arms from copper and bronze. Now a new world opened to them, and the clang of sledges re-echoed throughout the land.</> - The Hyborian Age\n\nMauls and warhammers are slow to swing and leave their user vulnerable to counterattack, but when they connect they are brutally effective. Armored foes are particularly vulnerable to these massive blunt weapons which break bones, shatter skulls and crush spines."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24107_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24251_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Deceiver"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24026_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24170_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\"> They stopped short. Conan faced them, not a naked man roused mazed and unarmed out of deep sleep to be butchered like a sheep, but a barbarian wide-awake and at bay, partly armored, and with his long sword in his hand.</> - The Phoenix on the Sword\n\nLongsword has become a catch-all phrase for the mongrel swords of a thousand different makes that don't align easily with one simple classification.\nThe only description of a longsword that seems to be agreed upon is that they are double-bladed and straight. Beyond that they vary wildly from grooved blades to smooth blades, long hilts to short hilts, one-handed and two-handed variations."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24026_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_24170_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Corrupting Brew"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_18215_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A foreboding liquid of acrid yet sweet aroma"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_18215_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<span style=\"italic\">Even the arts you call sorcery are governed by cosmic laws.</> - The People of the Black Circle\n\nFoul ingredients are brewed together to make this forbidden drink which corrupts body and soul. Sorcerers covet this libation, for they know that it nourishes a certain, long atrophied organ of the human soul, stimulating it to open like a nocturnal flower and become sensitive to the vibrations and blasphemies of the Outer Dark."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "HA_ItemTableOverwrites_18215_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "Throwing Axe of Nergal"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_50561_Name",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A throwing-axe crafted of a dull, grey metal that radiates with intense coldness. "
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_50561_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "This weapon traces its origins to a demon-haunted realm of shadow and ice ruled by Nergal, the Father of Bats. Artefacts from this terrible dimension are charged with Nergal's baleful hatred of all living things and radiate with supernatural coldness as a result. \n\nHeld in the off hand, these axes can be used for hacking at enemy shields and, in an emergency, hurled at their faces."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_50561_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
