  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "A twisted rope strong enough to drag a captive a short distance"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24134_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EAA_Recipes_5443451_ShortDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "<LoreItalics>How long Conan lay senseless he never knew. His first sensation of returning consciousness was that of being dragged by one arm over rough and stony ground, and through dense underbrush. Then he was thrown carelessly down, and perhaps the jolt brought back his senses.</> - The Hour of the Dragon\n\nRopes have dozens of uses, but the most common in the Exiled Lands is the binding and capture of thralls. Once an enemy is rendered unconscious, their ankles are bound with rope and they are dragged into captivity.\n\nRopes abrade on sharp stones and unravel often. The stronger the material of the rope, the further the captive can be dragged."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_24134_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "The Tiger's Truncheon"
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_10095_Name",
     "Path": ""
    },
    {
     "Key": "DT_EAA_Recipes_5443450_RecipeName",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "Source": {
    "Text": "This truncheon once belonged to Jin-Zhao the Tiger, the leader of a ruthless slave-trader band. His legacy is not written upon scrolls or stones but endures in the traumatized memories of those who lost loved ones to his club's skull-crushing infamy.\n\nBorn a slave, Jin-Zhao claimed his fearsome title in the blood-soaked fighting pits of Khitai. There, amidst the roars and jeers of the bloodthirsty crowd, he battled a tiger as fierce as the emperor's wrath, wild and relentless. The fight left Jin-Zhao victorious but marked by the beast's claws in ragged lines that strangely evoked the tiger's own stripes and forever proclaimed his ferocity.\n\nIf asked whether it is better to be loved or feared, Jin-Zhao would undoubtedly choose fear, for in the harsh lands of Khitai, fear serves as the sharpest weapon."
   },
   "Keys": [
    {
     "Key": "ItemTable_10095_LongDesc",
     "Path": ""
    }
   ]
  },
